    "poster_id": 1991,
    "post_rendered": "Find the smallest prime number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"11\" > that cannot be represented in the form <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/b/aab3f964a0bfe234ccfc53896820f68d2585210c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|3^{a} - 2^{b}|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"20\" >,</span> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\"  width=\"9\" height=\"8\" > and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\"  width=\"8\" height=\"12\" > are non-negative integers.",
    "post_canonical": "Find the smallest prime number $p$ that cannot be represented in the form $|3^{a} - 2^{b}|$, where $a$ and $b$ are non-negative integers.",
