    "poster_id": 1991,
    "post_rendered": "21 people take a test with 15 true or false questions.  It is known that every 2 people have at least 1 correct answer in common.  What is the minimum number of people that could have correctly answered the question which the most people were correct on?",
    "post_canonical": "21 people take a test with 15 true or false questions.  It is known that every 2 people have at least 1 correct answer in common.  What is the minimum number of people that could have correctly answered the question which the most people were correct on?",
