   "post_data": {
    "post_id": 234867,
    "post_type": "forum",
    "topic_id": 37598,
    "poster_id": 1991,
    "post_rendered": "Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/f/20f3ce862d15055dd7d002312fbcbb50fd4cab64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S = \\lbrace A = (a_1, \\ldots, a_s) \\mid a_i = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"234\" height=\"18\" > or <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/d/48dea1f8bab58af7588d705bbdb786d62760501f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1, i = 1, \\ldots, 8 \\rbrace$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"114\" height=\"18\" >.</span>  For any 2 elements of <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\"  width=\"12\" height=\"12\" >,</span> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/f/5cf9d5b23ec619a2b91cc49875489b5b0f982c4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = \\lbrace a_1, \\ldots, a_8\\rbrace$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"129\" height=\"18\" > and <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/e/32e63f0dee6800ff2ba6c7370da5944fbd5192f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B = \\lbrace b_1, \\ldots, b_8\\rbrace$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"127\" height=\"18\" >.</span>  Let <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/c/66cbc54463d6bdb7fd263ff0e7a0e2f47d8f09d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d(A,B) = \\sum_{i=1}{8} |a_i - b_i|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"181\" height=\"38\" >.</span> Call <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/3/9f3a2cfbf27f65e23f86ce720525fafdf2ed8ba0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d(A,B)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"58\" height=\"18\" > the distance between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\"  width=\"13\" height=\"13\" > and <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\"  width=\"14\" height=\"12\" >.</span>  At most how many elements can <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\"  width=\"12\" height=\"12\" > have such that the distance between any 2 sets is at least 5?",
    "post_canonical": "Let $S = \\lbrace A = (a_1, \\ldots, a_s) \\mid a_i = 0$ or $1, i = 1, \\ldots, 8 \\rbrace$.  For any 2 elements of $S$, $A = \\lbrace a_1, \\ldots, a_8\\rbrace$ and $B = \\lbrace b_1, \\ldots, b_8\\rbrace$.  Let $d(A,B) = \\sum_{i=1}{8} |a_i - b_i|$. Call $d(A,B)$ the distance between $A$ and $B$.  At most how many elements can $S$ have such that the distance between any 2 sets is at least 5?",
